diagnosis_text:
The affected component is the campus DNS resolver on srv1 (BIND/named). User traffic from the WiFi VLAN is fine at L2/L3, but name resolution is broken, which makes “nothing work” for typical applications. From laptop1 (10.6.0.100) we can ping its gateway 10.6.0.1 (MAC 5a:f2:88:92:1a:ab on dswa2 br0) and reach other subnets (e.g., pc1 10.1.0.100 and pc3 10.3.0.100). Both laptop1 and pc1 point to nameserver 10.5.0.4 (srv1), yet getent hosts example.com returns RC=2 (failure). On srv1, named is listening on 10.5.0.4:53, but /etc/bind/named.conf.options has the forwarders block commented out. The lab’s “internet” is not generally reachable (srv1 ping to 8.8.8.8 yields TTL exceeded), so recursive resolution via root server
